    Q('perm-order', 'Settings and hooks', 'm',
      'In what order are permission rules checked, and which settings file wins?',
      'Deny, ask, allow. Then think from managed down to user.',
      'Rules are checked deny first, then ask, then allow, so a deny always wins. Settings files are merged with managed settings highest, then command line, then .claude/settings.local.json, then .claude/settings.json, then ~/.claude/settings.json. Permission rule lists are merged across files rather than replaced.',
      '<pre>{\n  "permissions": {\n    "allow": ["Bash(pytest *)"],\n    "deny": ["Read(./.env*)", "Bash(git push --force *)"]\n  }\n}</pre>'),
